WEBVTT

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:08.460
Ever since I was a child,
I felt like there were walls up.

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:09.960
Year

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:13.260
They would...

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:18.390
...hem me in and prevent me
from doing whatever I wanted.

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:23.560
High, unseen walls.

00:00:27.770 --> 00:00:33.240
I wanted to climb over those walls...
so I began living on my own.

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:44.670
Then, after that...

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:13.530
Long time.

00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:18.530
Welcome. Come on in.

00:02:53.590 --> 00:02:55.090
Be my guest.

00:03:21.820 --> 00:03:24.830
Have a seat anywhere.
I'll make us some tea.

00:03:24.830 --> 00:03:26.240
I'd rather have water instead of tea.

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:28.000
You got it.

00:03:34.250 --> 00:03:35.460
Here.

00:03:35.460 --> 00:03:36.920
Thanks.

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:45.430
What would you like for supper?
What do I even have, anyway?

00:03:45.430 --> 00:03:47.810
I just got back here today,
so there isn't much of--

00:03:47.810 --> 00:03:49.020
I bought us something.

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:50.270
Huh?

00:03:50.270 --> 00:03:53.270
I'll make it now.
Let me use your kitchen.

00:03:55.980 --> 00:03:57.980
What are you making for us?

00:03:57.980 --> 00:04:01.450
<i>Okonomiyaki. </i>Unless you don't like it.

00:04:01.450 --> 00:04:05.910
Hmm! I love <i>okonomiyaki</i>!

00:04:08.240 --> 00:04:10.160
They're done. Let's eat.

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:13.460
Mm, thank you for this food!

00:04:13.460 --> 00:04:15.210
Thank you for this food.

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:19.170
Mm, it's good!

00:04:26.180 --> 00:04:28.930
So, did that job of yours go all right?

00:04:28.930 --> 00:04:32.520
Mm-hmm. It went smoothly. How about you?

00:04:32.520 --> 00:04:34.390
Hmm?

00:04:34.390 --> 00:04:38.230
Where did you go for summer vacation?

00:04:38.230 --> 00:04:40.400
I told you before, didn't I?

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:43.150
Somewhere close... yet far away.

00:04:43.150 --> 00:04:48.160
Episode 5

00:04:43.150 --> 00:04:48.160
Super Cub

00:04:43.150 --> 00:04:48.160
Reiko's Summer

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:10.390
Back it up, back it up,
back it up... Stop!

00:05:10.390 --> 00:05:11.930
Okay, start loading!

00:05:11.930 --> 00:05:14.270
Right.

00:05:14.270 --> 00:05:16.270
Here it comes...

00:05:24.190 --> 00:05:29.370
...three, four, five, six,
seven, eight, nine, ten...

00:05:29.370 --> 00:05:32.020
The amount of supplies
is increasing, huh?

00:05:30.580 --> 00:05:33.290
Chief, the count is right.

00:05:33.290 --> 00:05:34.250
Okay.

00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:37.170
Well, I'm going to go check the trail.

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:40.040
There's still plenty of time,
so don't rush it.

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:41.300
Drive safely.

00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:44.460
Right. I'll drive safely.

00:05:51.390 --> 00:05:52.810
Okay...

00:06:45.320 --> 00:06:47.280
Damn it!

00:06:58.330 --> 00:07:01.830
The summer of my second
year in high school,

00:07:01.830 --> 00:07:05.840
I climbed Mt. Fuji on my Super Cub.

00:07:18.430 --> 00:07:21.190
Nothing out of the ordinary on the trail.

00:07:21.190 --> 00:07:23.520
Okay, good job.

00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:25.070
All right, let's go!

00:07:25.070 --> 00:07:26.780
Right.

00:07:29.510 --> 00:07:31.970
Mt. Fuji Subashiri
Trail Station 5

00:07:40.500 --> 00:07:42.980
Mountain Hut Kikuya

00:07:40.500 --> 00:07:43.080
Why are you doing this?

00:07:46.750 --> 00:07:51.760
I first became interested when I read
a book by a biker adventurist.

00:07:56.600 --> 00:08:02.060
Yeah, apparently, they used to climb
Mt. Fuji on motorbikes a lot back then.

00:08:02.060 --> 00:08:03.980
Can you not do it anymore?

00:08:03.980 --> 00:08:06.230
With environmental regulations
and mountain climbing rules,

00:08:06.230 --> 00:08:08.480
things are a lot more strict
now compared to before.

00:08:08.480 --> 00:08:11.110
Yeah, there's not much you can do.

00:08:13.320 --> 00:08:15.740
"Due to the treacherous
debris and steep slope,

00:08:15.740 --> 00:08:19.240
only a high-performance off-road
bike can make the climb."

00:08:22.620 --> 00:08:25.080
I guess it's out of the question.

00:08:25.710 --> 00:08:27.690
Super Cub off-road custom

00:08:35.260 --> 00:08:38.260
A CT110 Hunter Cub...

00:08:38.260 --> 00:08:44.390
That's it. I don't need to tweak Super
Cub parts; I could just use these.

00:08:54.320 --> 00:08:56.030
There.

00:09:00.120 --> 00:09:03.000
Still, even if I have the bike to do it,

00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:07.210
that doesn't mean I'm going to
get permission to climb Mt. Fuji.

00:09:07.210 --> 00:09:09.130
While you're working for us,

00:09:09.130 --> 00:09:12.010
you'll have to stay at an apartment
at the foot of the mountain.

00:09:12.010 --> 00:09:13.420
That's fine.

00:09:13.420 --> 00:09:15.430
Any mountain climbing experience?

00:09:15.430 --> 00:09:17.220
No, sir.

00:09:17.220 --> 00:09:19.220
Is that a requirement?

00:09:19.220 --> 00:09:24.940
No, not really. So, as for why
you want to work here...

00:09:24.940 --> 00:09:28.150
"I want to climb Mt. Fuji
on my motorbike."
Right, it's just as I've written there.

00:09:29.270 --> 00:09:33.740
I want to climb Mt. Fuji on my motorbike.

00:09:40.490 --> 00:09:43.410
Loading work starts tomorrow morning at 4.

00:09:43.410 --> 00:09:47.210
Also, I've decided to have
you do the trail checks.

00:09:47.210 --> 00:09:49.210
Trail checks?

00:09:50.710 --> 00:09:53.010
You have to check the weather
and surface conditions

00:09:53.010 --> 00:09:56.380
before the Caterpillar heads out.

00:09:56.380 --> 00:09:57.510
On <i>that</i>.

00:09:57.510 --> 00:09:58.260
Huh?

00:09:58.260 --> 00:10:01.680
And you only really have
to check up to Station 6,

00:10:01.680 --> 00:10:06.310
but if it's necessary, I won't mind
if you go up higher than that.

00:10:08.310 --> 00:10:11.060
Right! Thank you very much!

00:10:23.290 --> 00:10:26.120
Why are you doing this?

00:10:32.380 --> 00:10:34.760
I just want to know...

00:10:36.670 --> 00:10:40.640
...if I'm the kind of person who can
overcome something like that.

00:10:57.400 --> 00:10:59.780
Damn...

00:11:02.620 --> 00:11:05.990
Nothing out of the ordinary on the trail.

00:11:05.990 --> 00:11:07.540
Okay.

00:11:52.580 --> 00:11:54.630
Altitude sickness.

00:11:56.960 --> 00:12:00.050
Thank you very much.

00:12:00.050 --> 00:12:03.720
Sip it. Don't gulp it all down at once.

00:12:03.720 --> 00:12:05.140
Right.

00:12:09.540 --> 00:12:12.540
{=0}Summiting Everest

00:12:59.780 --> 00:13:01.780
Damn it...

00:13:03.610 --> 00:13:05.410
Damn it...

00:13:06.990 --> 00:13:10.830
Damn it...! Damn it...!

00:13:10.830 --> 00:13:14.410
Damn it, damn it, damn it...!

00:13:14.410 --> 00:13:16.750
Damn it!

00:13:18.420 --> 00:13:21.130
Damn... it...

00:13:26.970 --> 00:13:30.760
You can't stand yourself
up to the mountain.

00:13:30.760 --> 00:13:33.310
You have to bring yourself alongside it.

00:13:38.150 --> 00:13:41.320
Bring myself... alongside?

00:13:45.070 --> 00:13:49.950
Even in the summer, Mt. Fuji has a slight
blanket of snow at its summit.

00:13:49.950 --> 00:13:55.000
I thought it was such a pretty mountain.
I want to see it up close.

00:13:55.000 --> 00:13:57.620
No doubt if you look down on it
from somewhere even higher,

00:13:57.620 --> 00:14:00.210
it looks even prettier.

00:14:06.550 --> 00:14:08.640
After my string of failures
these last few days,

00:14:08.640 --> 00:14:10.850
I'd even forgotten how to smile.

00:14:12.720 --> 00:14:15.020
I was climbing Mt. Fuji on my Cub.

00:14:15.020 --> 00:14:17.480
Why, when I was doing something this fun,

00:14:17.480 --> 00:14:23.690
did it feel like I was being made to
suffer by some despicable enemy?

00:14:25.860 --> 00:14:29.280
I'm off to go check the trail.

00:14:29.280 --> 00:14:31.160
Drive safely.

00:15:05.110 --> 00:15:07.240
There's nothing wrong with the suspension.

00:15:07.240 --> 00:15:10.110
The frame is buckling
a tiny bit, but it's fine.

00:15:10.110 --> 00:15:13.910
The engine's electricals
and fuel are on the money.

00:15:13.910 --> 00:15:16.750
All that leaves is me!

00:15:19.290 --> 00:15:22.960
Damn...

00:15:26.710 --> 00:15:29.300
You can't stand yourself
up to the mountain.

00:15:29.300 --> 00:15:31.970
You have to bring yourself alongside it.

00:15:31.970 --> 00:15:37.060
That doesn't mean that you go limp
and give yourself over to the mountain;

00:15:37.060 --> 00:15:41.230
you have to hold yourself down
and fight as hard as you can!

00:15:41.230 --> 00:15:43.150
But this is tough, all right.

00:15:43.150 --> 00:15:44.610
You can do it! You can keep going!

00:15:44.610 --> 00:15:46.900
--This is crazy! I want to stop!
--I want to climb! I want to go higher!

00:15:46.900 --> 00:15:47.780
--Damn it!
--I want to climb! I want to go higher!

00:15:47.780 --> 00:15:49.070
I can't give up now!

00:15:49.070 --> 00:15:53.370
--I can always try again next year.
--You dummy! Keep on running!

00:15:54.410 --> 00:15:56.660
A Super Cub. A used one.

00:15:56.660 --> 00:16:00.960
Oh, a Cub? That's more of a scooter
than a motorbike, isn't it?

00:16:00.960 --> 00:16:03.710
You ride a Cub?

00:16:03.710 --> 00:16:06.130
Sitting on my Cub like this,

00:16:06.130 --> 00:16:09.260
it feels like I can go anywhere
I like, as far away as I like,

00:16:09.260 --> 00:16:12.890
even when I'm standing still.

00:16:12.890 --> 00:16:16.180
I haven't gone all that far away, so...

00:16:16.180 --> 00:16:21.190
You can go anywhere you want to.
I mean, you've got a Cub!

00:16:21.190 --> 00:16:23.520
Somewhere close, yet far away.

00:16:23.520 --> 00:16:25.310
Be careful, okay?

00:16:26.270 --> 00:16:27.610
Yeah.

00:16:31.240 --> 00:16:36.120
I don't have enough oxygen...
or hydration... But...

00:16:36.120 --> 00:16:41.120
...I told her... that she
could go anywhere...

00:16:41.120 --> 00:16:45.290
And after telling her that,
I can't very well stop here!

00:16:58.260 --> 00:17:01.100
Damn it!

00:17:38.970 --> 00:17:42.100
Yeah, I'm finished.

00:17:42.100 --> 00:17:46.190
Could I ask you to pick me up on
your way down from the summit?

00:18:03.410 --> 00:18:05.500
Thank you very much.

00:18:07.580 --> 00:18:10.590
You didn't get all the way to the top?

00:18:22.010 --> 00:18:25.850
Still, I don't feel too bad.

00:18:31.190 --> 00:18:32.480
That's silly.

00:18:32.480 --> 00:18:35.740
Yeah, you're right about that.
I was wondering, myself,

00:18:35.740 --> 00:18:39.160
why I would do something
as ridiculous as this.

00:18:40.160 --> 00:18:41.160
Mm!

00:18:41.160 --> 00:18:45.410
Riding your motorbike
to climb Mt. Fuji is silly.

00:18:47.080 --> 00:18:48.620
Mm-hmm.

00:18:56.970 --> 00:19:01.850
No way! I had no idea that your
Cub was the "Cursed Cub"!

00:19:01.850 --> 00:19:03.140
You know about it?

00:19:03.140 --> 00:19:05.020
Well, the stories, at least.

00:19:05.020 --> 00:19:07.890
It's said to have killed three people--

00:19:07.890 --> 00:19:09.310
Ridiculous.

00:19:09.310 --> 00:19:12.900
The old soba shop guy who first bought it
died from drinking too much.

00:19:12.900 --> 00:19:15.230
It had nothing to do with the Cub.

00:19:15.230 --> 00:19:18.570
The second guy, who ran a
bookstore, didn't even die;

00:19:18.570 --> 00:19:20.820
he got into so much debt, he skipped town.

00:19:20.820 --> 00:19:25.290
And the third one was a priest who lost
his license, and parted ways with it.

00:19:26.580 --> 00:19:28.460
Feel better now?

00:19:30.170 --> 00:19:34.960
Mm-hmm. But all three of them
sound like unsavory characters.

00:19:40.760 --> 00:19:42.300
Well, I should get going.

00:19:42.300 --> 00:19:43.550
Spend the night here.

00:19:43.550 --> 00:19:44.560
Huh?

00:19:44.560 --> 00:19:48.430
There are no streetlights out here,
so it's pitch-black at night.

00:19:51.400 --> 00:19:52.600
Here!

00:20:13.040 --> 00:20:16.800
Maybe... it really was
a silly thing to do.

00:20:16.800 --> 00:20:19.130
Mm-hmm. Silly.

00:20:19.130 --> 00:20:25.550
I can't believe you fell off partway up.
My Cub would have made it up to the top.

00:20:27.810 --> 00:20:30.390
There's no way that would happen.

00:20:30.390 --> 00:20:35.190
It's simply impossible to climb up
Mt. Fuji on a Cub. There's no way.

00:20:37.570 --> 00:20:41.740
It's silly, but I don't think it's
something that <i>can't </i>be done.

00:20:45.700 --> 00:20:46.620
Mm-hmm.

00:20:46.620 --> 00:20:49.910
It was August of 1963.

00:20:49.910 --> 00:20:55.330
A mountain climbing and bike enthusiast
who lived in Yamanashi Prefecture

00:20:55.330 --> 00:20:59.130
successfully climbed Mt. Fuji via
the Fujinomiya trail on a Super Cub.

00:20:59.130 --> 00:21:02.590
Then, that same year,
the curator of Ueno Zoo

00:21:02.590 --> 00:21:05.340
successfully made the climb up Mt. Fuji

00:21:05.340 --> 00:21:08.390
using a composite team of
Hunter Cubs and Monkeys.

00:21:08.390 --> 00:21:11.140
And next, so will I.

00:21:27.450 --> 00:21:29.030
Here.

00:21:29.030 --> 00:21:30.580
Thanks.

00:21:31.830 --> 00:21:35.830
What about the rest of your summer
vacation? We still have one week.

00:21:35.830 --> 00:21:40.050
I'll fix up my Cub.
What do you have in mind?

00:21:40.050 --> 00:21:41.800
I'm thinking of getting my license.

00:21:41.800 --> 00:21:44.930
Your license? A full motorcycle one?

00:21:44.930 --> 00:21:48.180
Having just a Class I license is
holding me back in some ways.

00:21:48.180 --> 00:21:51.350
I see. So that's what your job was about.

00:21:51.350 --> 00:21:52.640
Mm-hmm.

00:21:52.640 --> 00:21:56.140
I'm going to get a motorcycle license.

00:21:56.140 --> 00:22:00.570
All right. Well, you'll need to make
a reservation right away.

00:22:01.650 --> 00:22:02.990
Huh?

00:22:05.950 --> 00:22:07.780
Wait, what reservation?

00:22:07.780 --> 00:22:10.120
With a driving school, of course.

00:22:10.120 --> 00:22:12.870
We'll have to soup up your engine, too.

00:22:12.870 --> 00:22:16.670
There's no point in getting your license
and staying with a 50cc engine.

00:22:18.210 --> 00:22:20.460
I can't handle anything too expensive.

00:22:20.460 --> 00:22:22.630
Then how about modding your block?

00:22:22.630 --> 00:22:23.920
Mod my block?

00:22:23.920 --> 00:22:25.010
Yep.

00:22:25.010 --> 00:22:27.840
You take the slight imperfections
in your engine block

00:22:27.840 --> 00:22:30.850
specific to cast iron combustion
chambers and cylinder heads,

00:22:30.850 --> 00:22:33.520
and, using equipment more precise
than what's on the production line,

00:22:33.520 --> 00:22:36.480
re-bore them out to be exactly circular,
then install oversized pistons to--

00:22:36.480 --> 00:22:37.810
Reiko!

00:22:37.810 --> 00:22:39.440
Hmm?

00:22:39.440 --> 00:22:42.610
Sorry, I'm not sure what you mean.

00:22:42.610 --> 00:22:46.700
Gotcha. Okay, let me explain it
clearer from the beginning.

00:22:46.700 --> 00:22:49.200
You see, mass-produced engines are...

00:24:10.930 --> 00:24:15.930
Super Cub

00:24:10.930 --> 00:24:15.930
Episode 6

00:24:10.930 --> 00:24:15.930
My Cub

00:24:12.660 --> 00:24:15.910
Episode 6: "My Cub."
